WEBVTT

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.350
I'd say we're looking pretty good.

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:16.940
We're not stumbling around anymore.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.900
We've definitely improved...

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.480
But compared to LizNoir,
we are still way behind.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.400
The disparity is expected.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.770
Yeah...

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:29.900
But still, we need to surpass LizNoir, right?

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.440
Huh?

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.980
Oh? Did I just say something weird?

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.100
No, not at all.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.020
It sounded like something Kotono would say.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.730
Y-Yeah you're right.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.020
I agree with Sakura.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.270
We can put in more enthusiasm
than them, at least.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.190
Or else we'll never catch up.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.060
I-I agree!

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:54.440
But it doesn't mean we need to
blindly increase our training.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.440
Let's come up with a smart strategy together.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.690
Yeah.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:00:59.850
Yes.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.900
How about a different group's choreography?

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:03.520
We might discover something new.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.190
Any groups you recommend?

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.020
I know.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:11.270
How are the fledglings doing upstairs?

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:15.730
The joint lesson with LizNoir
boosted their motivation quite a bit.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:17.060
As I expected.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:21.310
They were bound to feel something
practicing alongside real idols.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.060
Did you foresee this happening?

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.980
It just turned out this way.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.560
But it was good timing.

